    "https://cps.unh.edu/online/why-unh-cps-online/career-support": {
      "title": "Career Support",
      "description": "Career Support | Online Skip to main content University of New Hampshire College of Professional Studies Search Menu Search UNH.edu Search College of Professional Studies Search UNH.edu Search Search Commonly Searched Items: Academic Calendar Visit Tuition Registrar Online Academics Associate Degrees Bachelor’s Degrees Three-Year (90 credit) Applied Bachelor's Degrees Master’s Degrees Post-Baccalaureate Teacher Licensure Minors Academic Catalog Early College Online Why UNH CPS Online Affordable Tuition Online Flexibility Respect for Prior Learning & Transfer Credit Military & VA Friendly Expert Faculty Personalized Advising Career Support Student Success Blog Accreditations and Achievements Employer partnerships & tuition benefits Apply & Register Apply Now Transfer Credit Evaluation Take a Course Community College of the Air Force Military and Veterans Benefits Calendars Accepted Students Registrar Tuition & Aid Tuition & Fees Types of Aid Eligibility Requirements FAFSA Financial Aid Resources Military and Veterans Benefits Tuition Waivers & Discounts Billing & Payments Resources Access My Accounts Current Students Bookstore Resources for Alumni Resources for Faculty & Staff Resources for School Counselors Employer Partnership Request CWEP Faculty & Staff Directory Highlights and News Technology Help Desk Support Contact Us Home Online Why UNH CPS Online Career Support In This Section Why UNH CPS Online Affordable Tuition Online Flexibility Respect for Prior Learning & Transfer Credit Military & VA Friendly Expert Faculty Personalized Advising Career Support Student Success Blog Accreditations and Achievements Employer partnerships & tuition benefits Career Support We're Here to Support Your Career Goals At the UNH College of Professional Studies, we're focused on supporting adult students like you. We are very motivated to make sure that you get an education that will work for you and provide opportunities for your personal and professional growth. Our student community includes adults at every stage of career development and our team is prepared to meet you where you are on your personal career path. Whether you are a career launcher (just starting your career), changer (looking to change industries or professions), or advancer (seeking to advance or modernize your skills), everyone can benefit from individualized career planning. Exploratory Advising Exploratory advising is a process that focuses on cross-curricular academic advising, career assessment, and guided exploration of major options. If you're new to UNH CPS Online and would like to meet with our Academic Advisor and Career Specialist, call us at (855) 472-4255 . Career and Professional Success (CaPS) The best time to start planning your career is right now. You'll find that we provide support and guidance to make your per­sonal goals a reality. Our expert team at UNH Career and Professional Success (CaPS) will guide you through a step-by-step process to learn more about your unique goals and connect them to tangible career milestones. We’ll introduce you to some free online career planning tools. Together, we can use the results in a one-on-one career counseling session to help you determine the right educational path and develop a personalized career action plan. Learn More About career services Internships, Practicums, and Capstones At the College of Professional Studies, our community is comprised of working adult students so we design our degree programs to integrate with your career and goals. There are several types of courses at the College that incorporate work experience. Current students work with their faculty member and advisor to determine the best option for their unique goals. The most common types of opportunities you’ll encounter include: Internships During internships, students work at a company, school, agency, or organization on an assignment or project that lasts up to an academic term in duration. Practicums Similar to an internship, a practicum is a course that requires both classroom time and several hours of work in the field at a company, school, agency, or organization. Integrative Capstones This is the final course students take in their degree program. The coursework integrates the concepts, outcomes, and knowledge gained throughout the duration of the degree program, with a culminating project, research, or internship experience that demonstrates what the student has learned. Career Development Course Career Development and Planning (APST 505) is a two-credit course, appropriate for all degree programs, address the particular concerns of adults at various stages of career development. Students will discover the conditions that guide career planning decision and give shape to individual careers. Topics covered include career and interest assessments, job search skills, resume and cover letter development, interview preparation, networking, and more. To register for this course, ask your advisor or consult the course to see when it’s offered next. View Course Schedule Career Ready: UNH CPS & Workforce Connections At the UNH College of Professional Studies, our programs blend academic best practices with a practical approach aligned with industry demands and the schedules of working professionals. Dynamic program curriculums allow you to take what you learn from the classroom into the field to directly apply your education in your work. Success Stories No matter your career stage, everyone can benefit from career advising! \"Before working with Career Services, I figured my resume was fine. It just wasn’t great. I was pleasantly surprised to learn that there were things I could do to make immediate improvements that I have since applied to my resume!\" - SANDRA HICKEY '17 \"Four months following graduation, I was hired as a Director of Diversity & Inclusion. This was a HUGE career bump for me. More importantly, I’m doing exactly what I envisioned myself doing when I started my program.\" - LYNDELE VON SCHILL '15 quick links Academics Apply & Register Tuition & Aid Why UNH CPS Online More to Explore Student Success Blog Resources Take a Course View Course Schedule Copyright © 2026, University of New Hampshire. All rights reserved. TTY Users: 7-1-1 or 800-735-2964 (Relay NH) USNH Privacy Policies  • USNH Terms of Use  • Accessibility  • Statement of Nondiscrimination  • Jeanne Clery Act CONTACT US UNH CPS Online 88 Commercial St. Manchester, NH 03101 (855) 472-4255 Contact Us College of Professional Studies Online Academics Show Academics submenu Associate Degrees Bachelor’s Degrees Three-Year (90 credit) Applied Bachelor's Degrees Master’s Degrees Post-Baccalaureate Teacher Licensure Minors Academic Catalog Early College Online Why UNH CPS Online Hide Why UNH CPS Online submenu Affordable Tuition Online Flexibility Respect for Prior Learning & Transfer Credit Show Respect for Prior Learning & Transfer Credit submenu CCSNH Partnership Military & VA Friendly Expert Faculty Personalized Advising Career Support Student Success Blog Accreditations and Achievements Employer partnerships & tuition benefits Apply & Register Show Apply & Register submenu Apply Now Show Apply Now submenu Undergraduate Apply Now Graduate Apply Now International Students Transfer Credit Evaluation Show Transfer Credit Evaluation submenu Credit for What You Know Take a Course Community College of the Air Force Military and Veterans Benefits Calendars Accepted Students Show Accepted Students submenu Orientation Registrar Show Registrar submenu Add/Drop/Withdraw From a Course Enrollment Verification, Inactivation, & Withdrawal Forms & FAQs Requesting a Transcript Tuition & Aid Show Tuition & Aid submenu Tuition & Fees Show Tuition & Fees submenu Cost of Attendance Net Price Calculator Types of Aid Show Types of Aid submenu Scholarships and Grants Federal and State Grants Student Loans Show Student Loans submenu Federal Direct Loans Federal Work Study Managing Costs Pe